Yes, the bootloader absolutely must be unlocked before you flash any files like a patched boot image. If you try to run the flashing command on a locked bootloader, the PC terminal will reject it with an error (usually saying "Command not allowed" or "Flashing is not allowed in Lock State"). [1] 
Because you are using a Tecno Spark 8 (KG6k) running Android 11, unlocking the bootloader will erase everything on the phone. Back up your files first, then follow these prerequisites before using Method A:
