## Step 0: Unlock Your Bootloader First

   1. On your phone, go to Settings > My Phone.
   2. Tap Build Number 7 times until it says "You are now a developer!"
   3. Go back to Settings > System > Developer Options.
   4. Turn on both OEM Unlocking and USB Debugging.
   5. Plug your phone into your computer via a USB cable.
   6. Open your PC terminal (Command Prompt or PowerShell) inside your ADB/Fastboot directory and type:
   
   adb reboot bootloader
   
   7. Once your phone's screen shifts into Fastboot mode, run the unlock command:
   
   fastboot flashing unlock
   
   8. Look at your phone's screen. It will prompt you to press a volume key (usually Volume Up) to confirm the unlock. Press it.
   9. Your phone will wipe itself and reboot. Go through the initial setup wizard, re-enable Developer Options and USB Debugging. [2] 

