## Step 2: The Android 11 "vbmeta" Rule (Very Important)
Because the Tecno Spark 8 runs Android 11, flashing only a patched boot image can trigger a "Verification Error" bootloop. To prevent this, you should disable the Android verified boot flag alongside your boot image:

   1. Look into the exact same stock firmware folder where you found boot.img and grab the vbmeta.img file. Move it to your computer's Fastboot folder.
   2. Put your phone back into Fastboot mode.
   3. Run this exact command to flash the vbmeta while turning off its checks:
   
   fastboot flash vbmeta --disable-verity --disable-verification vbmeta.img
   
   4. Immediately after that, flash your patched Magisk file:
   
   fastboot flash boot magisk_patched.img
   
   5. Type fastboot reboot to finish. [3] 

